on sendFragmentToUrl (text, url, pikeIp, pikePort) {
	«Send a piece of text to a window that's opened for editing in Pike. The window is identified by its URL.
		«03/24/00; 12:34:00 AM by PBS
	
	«Here's the scoop:
		«All we have is the following: some text, the URL of a page that's being edited, and info about the person doing the editing -- we've got their IP address and the port their copy of Pike is listening on.
		«We shouldn't need anything else.
		«We'll just package up the params and send them to an XML-RPC handler inside Pike.
		«If Pike returns true, it worked. If Pike returns false, that means that window isn't open for editing. This script just returns the result to whoever called it.
	
	local (params = {text, url}); //simple, short
	local (procedureName = "pike.pasteFragment");
	
	local (result);
	result = betty.rpc.client (pikeIp, pikePort, procedureName, @params, fldebug:false);
	
	return (result)}